No external renderer or Go runtime dependency is bundled.

Additional research references (no implementation bundled):
- bmaupin/js-civ5save (MIT): setup-header scope and compatibility references.
- rivarolle/civ5-saveparser (MIT), commit bb4e825d005a0e5c4e4903ba29c4691fa0c78fcf:
  legacy header investigation.
- Gedemon/Civ5-DLL: SDK serialization declarations consulted as format evidence.
  SDK source carries separate game copyright; no SDK source is included or
  relicensed here. The experimental readers are experimental format implementations.
User game saves are local research inputs, not distributed assets.

Alliance format reference: EnormousApplePie/Lekmod, LEKMOD_DLL/CvGameCoreDLL_Expansion2/CvMinorCivAI.cpp and .h, consulted 2026-10-10. No Lekmod source code is bundled.
Capital/route format references: Gedemon/Civ5-DLL CvPlayer.cpp and CvPlot.cpp,
EnormousApplePie/Lekmod CvPlayer.cpp and CvPlot.cpp, and whoward69/DLL-VMC
CvPlayer.cpp, consulted 2026-10-10. Format evidence only; no source bundled.

Replay/map readers and event semantics adapt the reviewed MIT source revision
above, especially fileio/civ5replay.go, civ5map.go, civ5mapapi.go and civ5save.go.
Additional evidence: Lekmod CvGame.cpp and CvReplayMessage.cpp and Gedemon SDK
CvReplayInfo.cpp/CvReplayMessage.cpp, consulted 2026-10-10/11. No game SDK or
Lekmod source is bundled. Local upstream scenario JSON was used for validation
only and is not redistributed as a project fixture.

Unit format evidence: Gedemon/Civ5-DLL CvUnit.h/CvUnit.cpp, CvPlot.cpp,
CvPromotionClasses.cpp and FireWorks archive/vector declarations; and
EnormousApplePie/Lekmod CvUnit.h/CvUnit.cpp, consulted 2026-10-11. Declaration
order establishes unit identity prefixes; archive-tail/promotions layouts and
empirical per-DLL offsets are documented separately. No SDK/Lekmod source is
bundled or relicensed. Terrain/army rendering uses original TypeScript/SVG code.


TypeScript runtime dependencies are identified in package.json/package-lock.json.
Bundled WASM and browser dependency license notices are in third_party/runtime-LICENSES.txt.
Fallback DejaVu fonts are bundled under their preserved license in
third_party/fonts-LICENSE.txt. Saves are never distributed as part of the application.

Default browser metadata in assets/databases is a compact lookup subset derived
from the user-provided Civilization V / Lekmod caches. It contains identities,
terrain/route/feature types, RGB values, military attributes and English names,
without save state, artwork or unrelated game text. Source and output hashes are
recorded in assets/databases/manifest.json; scripts/prepare_browser_databases.mjs
reproduces the subset. Game and mod metadata retains its original ownership;
the project's MIT license applies to CivMapper code, not third-party game data.
